          "text": "{\"relation\":\"MATCH\",\"consensus_summary\":\"Garments primarily symbolize a person’s spiritual or moral condition before God, especially righteousness and salvation; clean or white garments signify righteousness, while filthy or defiled garments signify sin and guilt.\",\"book_summary\":\"Garments symbolize righteousness, specifically the righteous acts of the saints, while soiled garments signify bloodguilt and sin; nakedness is presented as the opposite.\",\"consensus_core_identification\":\"Garment = righteousness or moral-spiritual condition, with cleanliness and defilement marking righteousness and sin respectively.\",\"book_core_identification\":\"Garment = righteousness or righteous acts, with soiling marking sin and defilement.\",\"core_relation\":\"EQUIVALENT\",\"extension_relation\":\"SAME_CASES\",\"boundary_disagreement\":\"No material boundary disagreement. The book emphasizes righteous acts rather than spelling out the consensus’s broader language of salvation, acceptance, or imputed righteousness, but this is an expressly recognized form of the consensus reading and is not presented as excluding the others.\",\"material_contradiction\":\"None. Both identify garments with righteousness and their defilement with sin.\",\"rationale\":\"At minimum core, both readings make the same identification: garments represent righteousness or moral condition, and filthy or defiled garments represent iniquity. The book’s phrase “righteous acts of the saints” closely follows Revelation 19:8 and falls directly within the consensus rather than replacing its referent. Its designation of nakedness as the opposite is compatible with the broader clothing-versus-shame imagery noted by the consensus.\",\"citation_support\":\"STRONG\",\"strongest_objection\":\"The book could be read as narrowing righteousness specifically to the saints’ acts, whereas the consensus also includes divinely bestowed or imputed righteousness and salvific standing. However, the entry does not explicitly deny those applications, and righteous deeds are already a prominent consensus case.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}"
        }
